A||||36||TSPalmer||Watch out for those SQUIRRELS!!||||8||
Z||000000||TSPalmer||11-02-2001||09:03 AM||||Those little furry creatures are deadly!<P>I was on my way to work this morning and one zipped out in front of me!!! I hear this loud thump and look back to see not only the squirrel but the left half of my front air dam flopping around in the road.  It was already cracked, but I couldn't help laughing at the fact such a tiny creature had done so much damage to the car.<P>Oh well, just gives me a reason to look at a new front clip! <P>In other news...the squirrel was found to be quite crumpled...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>T.Shawn Palmer<BR>'85 SE 4cyl 5spd||||reg||8
Z||000001||California Kid||11-02-2001||09:55 AM||||I was out on my Ninja one day and ran over a dead one (saw it too late because of car in front of me). Lucky I wasn't too far from home because the front and rear tires went flat in the next hour.  There were squirrel ribs bones embedded in the tires!!!  Avoid them buggers if they are dead or alive!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-02-2001||10:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TSPalmer:<BR><B>...I couldn't help laughing at the fact such a tiny creature had done so much damage to the car.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry about the "killer squirrel".<P>You ought to see what a truck retread will do to a 1st gen RX-7 airdam.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Some mornings, it just isn't worth chewing through the restraints.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||TSPalmer||11-02-2001||10:46 AM||||That's why I try to dodge those critters. Never had one wipe out a tire, but I've heard about it happening.<P>The wife and I were coming home from the company Christmas party a few years back and I hit a dog on the interstate that did $1100.00 worth of damage to my then daily beater Honda Civic.  Took out the cheesy radiator, the oil pan and shoved the bumper backwards a good ways.  <P>I can only imagine what a slab of truck tire would do for you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Shawn||||reg||1
Z||000004||BlackStang95||11-02-2001||11:34 AM||||How could you not avoid a dog?  Idiot, that was prolly some kids pet.  I'm glad it messed your honduh up.||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||11-02-2001||11:38 AM||||Gieko insurance has a hilarious commercial with 2 squirrels. They even Hi-5 after crashing a car,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||11-02-2001||11:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>How could you not avoid a dog?  Idiot, that was prolly some kids pet.  I'm glad it messed your honduh up.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||13
Z||000007||TSPalmer||11-02-2001||11:50 AM||||Stang - I said it was on the interstate, I was doing 65 (at least).  As for the honda, it's now my Dad's daily beater with 221,000 miles on it and still running.  <P>Flame somewhere else  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000008||GodSend||11-02-2001||11:50 AM||||While I always try to avoid animals at all costs, on the freeway sometimes it is impossible.<P>My mother is perhaps the perfect example of a "grandma" type driver.  Never exceeds the speed limit, always allows lots of following distance , pretty much the works.  I can still remember being in he car with her on the 401 in Downtown Toronto .. 16 lanes of traffic, and a dog jumped out on the high way (made it all the way to the middle of the highway where we were).  We had no option but to just plow it over.  It was either hit the dog, or attempt to avoid possibly killing ourselves, and other people on the highway at the same time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroKyleatSchool||11-02-2001||11:53 AM||||Yeah, that insurance comercial is pretty funny.<BR>I hit a possum with the Fiero and that sucker stood up when it (at 85 mph) hit and the car ramped into mid air over the car and landed behind me. I pissed at first cuz I thought it might of did damage, but it didn't and now its funny to look back.<BR>The dog thing was accident I am sure he didn't mean to do it. Sh%t happens.<BR>Kills: 1 rabbit, 1 possum||||reg||6
Z||000010||TSPalmer||11-02-2001||12:02 PM||||Yeah that commercial is pretty funny!<P>The dog thing was on Hwy 220 (Future 73/74) about 2:00 in the morning.  It just appeared out in front of us.  I was walking back up the highway to check on it when the State Patrol showed up to see what had happend. Didn't have a collar or anything so I don't know who the dog belonged to.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
