Z||000013||BN Boomer||11-02-2001||12:41 PM||||I once hit and killed a dog in a freakin' school zone, right in front of a bunch of kids who were just getting out no less. I was only going about 20 but the dang dog darted out from between two parked cars and right in front of me. I only saw a small blur in the corner of the windshield before feeling the thump. Got out of my truck to find a dead German Shepperd pup and a bunch of kids staring in disbelief. Even though it wasn't my fault and there was nothing I could have done to avoid it, that sure felt like sh!t.<P>I guess blackstain doesn't to hear about the time I killed around 15 or so deer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Greg, aka Boomer<BR>Red 85 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.gmemd.com/locomotives/naf/images/sd70sm.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Butter||11-02-2001||12:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>How could you not avoid a dog?  Idiot, that was prolly some kids pet.  I'm glad it messed your honduh up.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Common Dude,<BR>Just cause you may have been on better odds than some of the rest of us don't mean you have to wish bad things on us.  By the way one of the Deer I accidentally hit was in my 1967 Ford Fairlane.  You think I wanted to mess up a classic car?  NO. ||||reg||8
Z||000015||Denny||11-02-2001||01:21 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TSPalmer:<BR><B>Stang's been doing ok lately, he just don't like Honda's....not a big deal, I heard it all the time.  People have opinions, don't mean we all have to agree or like that opinion.<P>Can't we all just get along.....LOL</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK, I withdraw my previous comment and apologize.  I've been away for a while, and the last comments I saw before leaving were pretty much argumentative, but I just did a search and you're right, he has been a good boy for the most part.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000016||fldevel||11-02-2001||03:39 PM||||i hit a dog once on my way home in my 85GT my lil 10 year old foster sister was with me at the time and she loves dogs ..the thing just darted out and just glazed the front left fender, i started fealing bad knowing that i had killed the dog with her in the car untill she twisted around as i kept goin and sed "stupid dog walked into you car" i just looked over and smiled ||||reg||1
Z||000017||84Bill||11-02-2001||03:55 PM||||Hit a bird once with my antenna. left behind a small clump of feathers on the ball tip, damndest thing I ever saw.||||reg||1
Z||000018||TSPalmer||11-02-2001||04:08 PM||||LOL 84Bill, my buddy hit an owl in his S-10 one night.  Left a fist sized hole in the plastic grill and feathers everywhere.||||reg||4
Z||000019||rogergarrison||11-02-2001||04:09 PM||||I did the same thing bill. In okla on turnpike, we were all half asleep in the middle of the nite and wham. Didnot know what it was untill i saw the goo and feathers on antenna.<P>Heres a perfect shot, a friend flying his plane one nite heard a big thump, but nothing showed up and everything was working fine. next morning he went to chk. theres a little probe on top of the windshield to read outside temps, he got a perfect bulls eye in a bat. speared him like a skewer,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>one time i was landing in zaynesville, ohio, and just when i got ready to touch down a big possum ran onto the runway, had to pour the power on and go back up.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Little Duce Coupe||11-02-2001||04:21 PM||||Had a friend once, his fiance tries to "miss" a dog that runs out in front of her by swerving.  Two wrecked parked cars and his truck totaled later she comes to a stop.... dog is ok but he ends up paying for it in his premiums for the next like 5 years and they end up divorced in the end anyway.<P>My moral is... if you can't keep from hitting an animal (small) while traveling in a straight line (by braking).... then Darwin was right!<P>My bad Fiero day.. I did hit a Peekanese (did I spell that right?) once.  I had glanced to the right and he ran accross the road from the left.  All I saw was a little brown blur flash in front of me as I turned my head back.  I started to "slam" on my brakes but then realized it had a better chance if I did'nt figuring if I did the front facia was gonna do him in for sure.<BR>Well the outcome is I hear bumpty bump and look in my mirror as I am slowing down only to see him spit out the back of my car doing cart wheels the dog is hopping around and yiping, looks like the worse he got was a broken front leg.<BR>.  Just then I see a lady running accross the street (apparently she had been chasing him) to pick him up and whisks him off shooting me dirty looks along the way.<P>Well.. thats my story, I only attach due the similarities of Peekanese and a squirels, and my refusal to sacrifice my car, my safety, or anyone elses for a Darwinian statistic.<P>Sorry... I really do love animals don't be too harsh.<P>2 cats<BR>2 fish tanks<BR>1 puppy coming soon this x-mas<P><P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||1
Z||000021||fierohoho||11-02-2001||05:19 PM||||I had a close call at the last Dells run. <P>We were on our way back to the Chula Vista in thoses curves when what had to be a 40 pound<BR>racoon ran in front of us.<P>Now normaly I will just brake in a straight line without trying to swerve but all I could think of was my new airdam I put on before leaving for the Dells.<P>I managed to swerve into the oncoming lane, just biffed the racoon with the right front tire, no damage to the car, the racoon? who knows.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||JSocha||11-02-2001||05:35 PM||||Dozens of squirrels.<BR>Tons of chipmunks, gophers, snakes.<BR>Gazillions of bugs   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Approximately 15-20 skunks.<BR>Birds...lost count<BR>3 bats.<BR>8 cats<BR>1 fox pup<BR>1 Badger...but that was deliberate and I stopped the front tire of the one ton on him before grabbing the rifle and filling him full of lead...not only tought, but one mean SOB too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Several adult ducks as well as mud loons.<BR>Scores of Muskrats!<BR>Family of little baby ducklings   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> this summer.  Wife wiped out one half of the batch crossing the road at night, I the remaining half that she missed.<BR>1 porcupine<BR>No dogs.<BR>No Deer...although close several times.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 11-02-2001).]||||reg||9
