Z||000026||Gary W||11-02-2001||10:22 PM||||On the subject of squirrels (non-Fiero): I was on my way to work a few years back, when I saw a pickup in the opposing lane stopped for a squirrel who couldn't decide which way to go &lt;---&gt;&lt;---&gt;. What I didn't see was the *-hole coming up behind him doing about 50  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> . He swerved around the pickup, and hit me head-on. I was doing 35. His Exploder went up and over my Cavalier. Both completely totalled. It was hard to convince the State Cops that a squirrel had caused the devastation - the squirrel left the scene without damage. Exploder got a ticket for tailgating. Both insurance companies interviewed me 3 times. I now aim for squirrels.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Wannabe||11-03-2001||12:37 AM||||Squirrels are rats with furry tails. They are not worth swerving for. Somebody actually nailed one right in front of my house this morning, even though the speed limit is 20 mph.Dogs and their owners should know better. Honking your horn is actually very effective with most animals - except dogs. ||||reg||1
Z||000028||Back On Holiday||11-03-2001||10:22 AM||||I hit a dead racoon the other day, I was too close to the person ahead of me and couldn't avoid it, damn thing was SO big it hit the Rear subframe behind the oilpan - a loung BOOM... I was *hoping* I didn't have it stuck to the parking brake cable and was dragging it down the road leaving a nice red smear behind me....||||reg||1
Z||000029||Mattyman||11-03-2001||11:12 AM||||Well when I first got my Fiero, I was driving down the road following a new grand am.  We were going pretty slow and i was close to him. All of a sudden a ground hog(a very big one at that) rolled out from underneith his car and I couldnt avoid it so it went right under my Fiero.  I felt it scrape across the whole bottom of the car. I looked in my rear view and saw it rolling out from the back of my car.  I think he survived though.  Then a week after that a bird was flying in the same direction as me and got right infront of me.  Im pretty sure it went through the front facia then out by the radiator.  I dont think he suvived||||reg||1
Z||000030||Mattyman||11-03-2001||11:14 AM||||Oh yeah, I forgot.  My friend the sick kid he is spun tire on a dead squirrel with his old beat cavalier station wagon.  It was actually quite funny.||||reg||1
Z||000031||FieroKyle||11-03-2001||12:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMontreal:<BR><B> <BR>And the fiero still looks that good??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Probably keeps on trucking!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
