Z||000033||FieroKyle||11-03-2001||01:22 PM||||Suprised no one from the PETA forum flaming us and telling us how we are so mean to animals and how we should put pillows on our cars so it won't kill bugs and deer and squirrels. Then they will go on about how fishing is cruel. Then one of the members will have a 95 Mustang thats solar powered exclaiming how its so much faster than our Fieros. Then when all comes to an end, Cliff have 3 people banned and people still fighting tooth and nail.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||11
Z||000034||SLYGUY||11-03-2001||01:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mattyman:<BR><B>Oh yeah, I forgot.  My friend the sick kid he is spun tire on a dead squirrel with his old beat cavalier station wagon.  It was actually quite funny.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cavalier station wagon???<BR>Never seen one of those before. Only wagons we see here are for status, not practicality. Mercedes,Volvo and other yuppie ones.<P>My kids scream like the girls they are ever time I aim for the already run over a million times flat dead whatever it once was carcas in the road when they are in the truck. I'd take them in the fiero but it's not safe with only one seat belt for the two of them. Even in the truck you can still feel their bones as you run them over. I'd back up for another pass, but with traffic and all it might be dangerous and people would think I was disturbed or somethin' LOL<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000035||Tigger||11-03-2001||04:50 PM||||Squirrels are funny creatures...<P>They always seem to double back when crossing a road.  They can get 3/4 of the way across the road, hear the car coming, then will turn back around and get run over.  It's almost predictable.  If the thing just kept on running across it would have made it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>I try my best under any conditions to avoid hitting any animal dead or alive.<P>There are times where you just can't do anything about it and times you just have to hit them instead of causing a bigger accident.||||reg||1
Z||000036||rogergarrison||11-03-2001||05:01 PM||||a few more of my road kills. I hit a pheasant with a van I had, killed it  and threw it up n over thru the air. I stopped to see if it broke anything, and this guy behind me ran up and asked if id didnt want it could he have it??????I think he wanted to cook it. When I took my roadtrip a month or so ago with vette club this shitzu (ya thats how I spell it, lol) ran out from one berm and ran in and out of 3 of our cars and amazingly, not one of us hit it. I dont know if this counts, but I wacked a big duck on the lake with the bow of my jet boat. He misjudged, i was going faster than he could fly  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
